  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (  ) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9:00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, details for: (i). the provision of six additional and secure cycle spaces; and (ii). new bin/recycling stores, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The cycle spaces and bin/recycling stores shall be implemented as approved prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted and thereafter shall be made available for use at all times.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, details of the privacy screening along the western/side edge of each balcony/terrace hereby permitted shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The screening measures shall be implemented as approved prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted and thereafter shall only be repaired or replaced in accordance with the agreed details.",
    "Condition : 7 - Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, the four window panes on the eastern/flank elevation as shown on drawing no. 862-DG-XX02 shall be obscurely glazed up to a height of 1.7m above the floor of the room in which the window is installed and non-opening below this height, and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise in accordance with these requirements.",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, the local planning authority shall be informed of the agreed naming and numbering of the proposed dwellings so that arrangements can be put in place to ensure that, with the exception of Blue Badge holders, no resident of the development shall obtain a resident's parking permit.",
    "Condition : 9 - Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, apartments 1 and 3 shall be laid out in strict accordance with that shown on drawing no's 862-DG-0401C & 862-DG-0501C, and thereafter the kitchen shall remain in situ.",
    "Condition : 10 - No development shall take place until a Construction Management/Logistics Plan has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved Plan shall be adhered to throughout the construction period. The Plan shall include: \r\ni. a site plan showing details of access, storage, loading and turning; \r\nii. safeguarding measures that would be put in place to protect the existing building; \r\niii. provision for the parking of vehicles of site operatives and visitors; \r\niv. provisions for storage of plant and materials within the site; \r\nv. the erection and maintenance of security hoarding (where applicable); \r\nvi. measures to control the emission of dust and dirt during construction; \r\nvii. any illumination of the site during construction; \r\nviii. a scheme for recycling/disposing of waste resulting from construction works; \r\nix. contractor membership of FORS or similar.",
    "Condition : 11 - The car park to the rear of the building on site shall be accessible for servicing and delivery vehicles at all times."
  ],
